            <ArticleTitle>Electrophysiologic observations in survivors of out-of-hospital cardiac arrest related to ischemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>287-91</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report their experience with inducible ventricular arrhythmias as an endpoint for the selection of long-term prophylactic antiarrhythmic drug regimens. In this article, they evaluate the efficacy of these regimens in preventing subsequent sudden deaths.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
